


There are various scripts and GUI tools available to assist with hostlog decoding through clicking. However, these tools may frequently fail due to a range of underlying issues. This guide is intended to help you understand the decoding workflow behind the curtain and provide quick troubleshooting steps when limited support is available.

This page contains four parts:
    - pcap decoding to binary
    - Binary to vcc hdf5
    - Binary to zen hdf5
    - Common errors

pcap decoding to binary

pre-conditions: hostlog-client, pcap file to decode

run the following command in cmd under hostlog-client folder and replace the actual paths with the parts with {}

set_path.bat
hostlog.bat offline pcap-to-binary --output {folder-path} {path-to-pcap-file}




More flags can be used with the command line if needed

 Parse PCAP(s) to binary file(s).
 Definitions are needed in order to handle partial DCF messages, both when reading PCAPs and writing complete messages to binary
 files. If definitions cannot be extract from given PCAPs, then definitions must be provided using option '--definitions'. Default
 output is a single binary file. If file size grows above 1GB, the file is split into additional file(s). The output file name
 indexed to indicate order of creation.
 N.B. PCAP_PATH supports CSV for both files and/or directories. Given files will be processed in the stated order. Files scanned
 from given directories are sorted in natural order.

